1:"Today's weather for One Han City looks sunny, with temperatures ranging between 27° and 34°. Some areas will see light showers around noon, but everyone is reminded to wear sunscreen if going outside." The dulcet voice of the weather reporter emanating from the television keeps reminding me that we have entered the hottest part of the year.
2:Just as I am thinking about my schedule for the day, my phone vibrates and a message from the Mahjong group chat pops up.
3:Furikomi Master
4:{character: Furikomi Master} Big news! Big news!!! The air conditioning in the dojo is busted, and it's gonna take a full week to repair it. It's hotter than an oven in there, so definitely don't come here! Boy, I sure took one for the team there, didn't I?!
5:"Furikomi Master" is the most active admin of the Mahjong group chat. And the dojo he mentioned is the one I frequent, the Aqua Dojo. But playing Mahjong in a dojo without air conditioning, in this weather...? Maybe I should find something else to do.
6:Like... Checking in on A-37? The idea pops into my head when my gaze falls upon some coupons on the coffee table.
7:A-37's been working part-time at that café near Central Park that went viral—"Éternité"—and brought a few coupons back yesterday. He said they're holding a special summer promotion, and that I should swing by if I had time.
8:Well, no time like the present! Let's go check it out.
10:
11:???
12:{character:???} Master... Master, this way, nyaa—
13:I look where the sound is coming from, only to see a hand waving frantically above the crowd. Occasionally, a little hop brings a pair of cat ears into view. Sure enough, it's Ichihime.
15:Ichihime
17:player
18:{character:player} Is Kaavi here too?
19:Reina Nanami
21:Reina Nanami half opens the door to the coffee shop, and cool air smelling sweetly of fresh coffee and cream hits my senses. I suppose I can see why Éternité has become so popular all of a sudden. In this sort of weather, who could possibly refuse a quality coffee shop offering not only special promotions, but also fully functioning air conditioning?
22:Inside, Éternité is not ostentatious at all, but decorated in a minimalist and comfortable modern style. The designers had made good use of plants and other furnishings to subtly divide the tables, offering customers a degree of privacy.
25:{character:player} This is...
29:{character:Ichihime} Master successfully captured! Nyaa!
30:Several recent crime news flashes through my head as I assess the strength of the two girls in front of me... I must have misunderstood the situation...
32:{character:Reina Nanami} Don't be so nervous! We just want to see if you'd be willing to come and help out at the shop for a while? We'd pay you by the day, of course!
34:{character:player} But... Don't you have enough part-time workers already?
36:{character:Reina Nanami} Ahaha... Well, now you brought it up, that might just be one of the reasons why we are short of staff.
37:Reina fishes out her phone, opens the forum homepage, and hands it to me—The whole screen is filled with posts about Éternité.
41:{character:Ichihime} Seems Master has understood our current predicament! So quick, go get changed and help Ichihime make some money, nyaa!
43:{character:Reina Nanami} And don't worry about the size of the uniform. It's all adjustable within a certain range.
45:{character:Ichihime} Oooooh, Ichihime can't wait to see how Master looks in the uniform, nyaa!
46:Declining is clearly not an option... But, you know what? The dojo's air conditioning was going to take ages to fix anyway, so why don't I take this time and see what's like to work in a popular café?
47:15 minutes later
50:Check out the cat tree over in the corner
51:See what's behind the nearby plants
60:I decide to check out the cat tree in the corner. And when I get closer I realize A-37 is indeed there. He is squatting down and giving a few of the cats a thorough brushing.
61:I'd have to thread my way through the whole café to actually get to the cat tree. To avoid such hassle, I decide to go have a look behind the nearby plants.
79:Hinata Takanashi grabs me and gives me a good look-over to see if I'm alright, before heaving a sigh of relief.
92:I look up and see Ichihime running back and forth at the counter. Yep, I probably count as a qualified cat owner.
94:Although A-37 had spoken in all seriousness, it is hard to imagine how this adorable British Shorthair—perching on my knee and swishing its tail gently against my arm—can be the dangerous creature he described.
98:I look down and examine more carefully, only to find there really is a pattern of 6-Sou! A-37 hands me the nearby kitty claw clipper, and I carefully probe the cat's front paw. Sure enough, Sixsou doesn't resist.
99:Squeezing the soft little pad gently, I can see four potentially formidable claws already protruding. I quickly trim each of them in turn, after which Sixsou glances up at me with an expression that seems to signify satisfaction with my service.
100:I manage to finish the job quickly, thanks in no small part to Sixsou's cooperation. Looking up, I see A-37 busy trimming the claws of a corpulent tabby. Catching my eye, he starts to introduce the kitty to me without looking up.
102:Simples is nowhere near as cooperative as Sixsou. As A-37 touches its hind leg, I see Simples twist its head and looks like it's about to bite. But, upon discovering that the offending touch comes from A-37, the tabby seems to think better of it and shrinks back in fear. This happens several times, until A-37 completes the job.
105:I look at A-37, then at the cat next to me. Suddenly, a bold idea strikes me, and I poke A-37 in the leg. A-37 jerks, his whole body visibly tensing as he looks at me with a panicked expression.
106:A-37 must have seen me gearing up to poke him again, as he promptly gets up and scarpers.
108:Looking at his retreating back, I begin to see why I didn't find it weird to see him in the middle of a bunch of cats.
111:I look at the small white cat, Haku, lying by A-37's feet and stretching out its pink little paws to snag his clothes. A-37 bends down and picks it up in one hand before stroking its head and handing it to me.
113:I carefully place the cat—more of a kitten, really—on my lap. It has long white fur, but there are shades of gray on its ears and the tip of its tail.
115:A-37 calls its name in a soft voice, then extends a finger to rub its chin. In response, Haku delicately places its paw in the palm of his hand.
119:A-37 lowers his head to clip Haku's claws, while telling me its history. His tone may be calm, but the story he told was truly sad.
120:I remember that I don't actually know that much about A-37. Sometimes an individual's past or their mood is easily expressed in their words, just like A-37 right then. Thinking of this, I stroked the kitten's furry head and decided to tell him what I was thinking.
122:A-37 seems surprised to hear me say this. He looks up at me, his golden eyes showing a touch of confusion, before quickly giving me a pure, clear smile.
128:Chiori picks up a deck of cards from a neighboring table and hands it to me.
131:I look at the figures scurrying busily around me, and then at the card in my hand. So Éternité is actually this kind of café? Before I can really think about it, Chiori grabs me by my sleeve.
133:I carefully read the instructions on the card. It's just a simple fun game, nothing too technical. If it's just Chiori and myself, we should be able to solve the problem with rock, paper, scissors.
136:To avoid disturbing others, we decide to go to the staff lounge next door to practice Truth or Dare.
138:Choice: Rock / Scissors / Paper
