179:Right when we are about to get back to the training, there is a knock at the door, and Reina Nanami comes in.
186:Reina and I glance at each other. Although Chiori seems angry, that seems to be what happened! Despite the misunderstanding, thanks to Riu I still had a busy and enjoyable afternoon.
188:Before I know it, the day is over. Even though my aching muscles are a constant reminder that I'd actually done a lot today, I am really happy. I forget who it was that said: Working is a pleasure, if you're working with those you like.
194:Choice: Truth / Dare
197:A random card is pulled from the "Truth" deck, which reads: When you are playing Mahjong with friends, would you discard tiles they need intentionally to make them happy?
198:Isn't that a bit too sensitive for an opening question?! But I think if it were me...
199:Choice: Yes / No
201:A random card is pulled from the "Dare" deck, which reads: Leave your current location and pat the first person you encounter on the head three times.
203:I reluctantly leave the gloating Chiori and push open the door, only to bump into Momo Hina!
211:I reach out and gently pat Momo on the head three times. Her hair is as soft and fluffy as her personality. But unfortunately, she wasn't able to join in our game and quickly returns to her busy work.
212:I look at myself and Chiori and all I can see are two really lazy workers... Never mind, it's better to be properly trained first before starting to work anyway.
224:I take a card fallen beside the stack Chiori pointed at and handed it to her.
226:Chiori leans over, staring at me with wide eyes, and starts counting down in a whisper: "30... 29... 28..."
227:However, to my surprise, after just ten seconds, her eyes are already turning red! That, coupled with the bow on her hair, makes her seem like a little rabbit.
228:With less than half the time left, she gives up unwillingly.
231:A random card is pulled from the "Truth" deck, which read: Would you choose the one in front of you if you need a teammate in a survival game?
